5.4 Treat the Zr atoms described in 5.2 as the coordinating atoms of Au, and the Zr and Au atoms described in 5.3 as the coordinating atoms of Zr. For each coordination polyhedron in the crystal, connecting its center to all of its vertices produces a number of small tetrahedra. State:
(1) the number of faces of the coordination polyhedron around an Au atom;
(2) the number of faces of the coordination polyhedron around a Zr atom;
(3) the number of coordination polyhedra that contain each small tetrahedron;
(4) the number of small tetrahedra in one unit cell.
